tatement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:1f0ca09e6026c774e7b3bfffd9be56fceb270ef0e22e4c931637e6d174e989f6","file":"preprints/Exact-Derandomization-of-Logarithmic-Space-L-equals-RL-equals-BPL-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":40,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"3d602d03e9ccdb8c6fba9a4229358a3391770b015afd89fcc9054ff50a53bf85","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Exact-Derandomization-of-Logarithmic-Space-L-equals-RL-equals-BPL-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:1f0ca09e6026c774e7b3bfffd9be56fceb270ef0e22e4c931637e6d174e989f6","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Exact-Derandomization-of-Logarithmic-Space-L-equals-RL-equals-BPL-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L40"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:probability}\nFix a randomized machine $\\mathcal M$ with polynomial worst-case\nrunning time and $O(\\log(n+2))$ work space. Let $p_{\\mathcal M}(x)$ be\nits acceptance probability on an input $x$ of length $n$. There is a\nuniform deterministic algorithm which, on input $(x,1^q)$ with $q\\ge1$,\noutputs an integer $0\\le a\\le2^{q+2}$ satisfying\n\\[\n       \\left|a2^{-(q+2)}-p_{\\mathcal M}(x)\\right|\\le2^{-q}.\n\\]\nIt uses $O(\\log(n+2)+q)$ work space and\n$(n+2)^{O(1)}2^{O(q)}$ time. The constants depend only on $\\mathcal M$."}
